    {
      "text": "workers. Thus, the average training runtime may vary by selecting different number of",
      "bbox": [
        89.60900115966797,
        183.0546112060547,
        521.8929443359375,
        192.68734741210938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "workers. The words E, and A represent exact-star and approx-star, respectively.",
      "bbox": [
        89.60900115966797,
        196.60362243652344,
        470.3365173339844,
        206.23635864257812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "4.1 12-Dimensional Quadcopter",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        221.694091796875,
        262.0479736328125,
        231.38137817382812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We consider the 12-dimensional quadcopter system under stochastic conditions for two",
      "bbox": [
        89.4469985961914,
        238.93707275390625,
        521.8988647460938,
        248.62435913085938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "different case studies. Trajectories are simulated using two ODE models from Hashemi",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        252.54063415527344,
        521.861083984375,
        262.1733703613281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "et al. (2024b) and Hashemi et al. (2024a) as our simulators. The state variables include the",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        266.08966064453125,
        521.8558959960938,
        275.7223815917969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "quadcopter’s position (x1, x2, x3), velocity (x4, x5, x6), Euler angles (x7, x8, x9) representing",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        279.5840759277344,
        521.9866943359375,
        290.33819580078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "roll, pitch, and yaw angles, and angular velocities (x10, x11, x12). We also include zero",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        293.1330871582031,
        521.9541015625,
        303.88720703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mean additive Gaussian process noise v ∼N(012×1, Σv) to the simulators with covariance",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        306.0721740722656,
        521.9569702148438,
        317.43621826171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Σv = diag",
      "bbox": [
        89.60700225830078,
        322.95208740234375,
        139.87583923339844,
        334.2753601074219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0010",
      "bbox": [
        141.87200927734375,
        317.9776306152344,
        148.38473510742188,
        324.95947265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[0.05 ×⃗11×6, 0.01 ×⃗11×6]]2\u0011",
      "bbox": [
        148.3870086669922,
        317.9776306152344,
        283.97979736328125,
        334.2892150878906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ". In both examples, the set of initial states s0 ∈I",
      "bbox": [
        283.98199462890625,
        322.3411865234375,
        521.20654296875,
        334.2753601074219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is taken from the cited papers, with the distribution s0 ∼W being uniform.",
      "bbox": [
        90.00003051757812,
